<details class="help-panel my-3"><summary>What do the record numbers mean?</summary><p>These numbers help you find the correct record, especially when two people have the same name.</p><ul><li><strong>BR:</strong> a person, for example BR-000001.</li><li><strong>LN:</strong> a loan.</li><li><strong>PAY:</strong> a payment.</li><li><strong>TXN:</strong> a saved entry in the money history.</li></ul><p>You do not need to type these numbers when adding a person or recording a payment. The app creates them for you. “Calculated” means the app worked out the interest automatically.</p></details>
